Contemporary English:

These are all Our verses, from before and from after. Thus, at that time, you yourself are Our complete proof, admitting whomever you will into the court of immense holiness.

This is how We begin, in every manifestation, a matter of the Cause from Our presence. Truly, We are sovereign in judgment. We never initiate a religion except for what shall be brought forth afterward, as a promise binding upon Us. Truly, We have power over all things.

We have made the gates of that religion equal to the number of all things, according to the number of the year, appointing for every day a gate through which souls may enter the supreme paradise. Let every number become a single remembrance of one letter from the First Letters, unto God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord of all things, Lord of what is seen and unseen, Lord of all worlds.

In the First Gate, We have ordained what God has testified concerning Himself: that there is no god but Him, the Lord of all things, and that whatever is besides Him is His creation, and all return unto Him.

The essence of the Seven Letters is the Gate of God for whoever is in the kingdoms of the heavens and the earth and whatever lies between them. Through the verses of God from Him do all find guidance.

Then, within every gate is the remembrance of a true name from Us, and the remembrance of one from the Letters of the Living, since they returned to their former spiritual lives: Muḥammad, the Messenger of God, and those who are witnesses from God.

Then come the gates of guidance, and they were created in the later creation according to what God promised in the Furqān, until the number of the One appears within the First Unity, as a grace from Us. Truly, We are bountiful.

This is the first unity of the numbered unities mentioned in the Month of Bahāʾ. We have now begun.

