Contemporary English:

That creation exists through Him, and We shall restore all things through Him, as a promise binding upon Us. Truly, We are powerful over all things.

I have numbered the numbers through that One in the first verse, and they appeared before Us with tranquil hearts in Our presence. Within it, nothing is seen except the One beyond all numbering. Thus does God clarify the measures of all things in the Book, so that people may give thanks in the days of their Lord.

O Pure Essence beyond all limitation: this Unity is that God—mighty and exalted—is and always has been in the exaltation of His eternal preexistence and the loftiness of His ancient being, while creation has always existed and continues to exist within the realm of contingent existence proper to itself.

In every age, God—glorious and exalted—has ordained and continues to ordain for creation a Book and a Proof. In the year 1270 from the mission of Muḥammad, the Messenger of God, He appointed the Bayān as the Book and the Essence of the Seven Letters as the Proof. He established the gates of the religion according to the number nineteen, forming a unity.

In the First Unity, He ordained the oneness of the Essence, the attributes, the actions, and the worship of God. As the guide to this Gate, He appointed “He Whom God Shall Manifest” and His Letters of the Living. Before His manifestation, He appointed the Essence of the Seven Letters together with His Letters, who had taken precedence in affirming divine unity.

This Unity is itself the same Unity found in the Qurʾān, which has existed in its outward and inward meanings, its firstness and lastness, and as the divine proof.

