... has been revealed in the Bayān—through it you establish whatever you desire. Then in the second: none knows the knowledge of the Bayān except you in your latter state and then your former one, or whoever bears witness to what I intend therein. Those are the ones who attain victory.

Then in the third: I have not permitted anyone to interpret except according to the interpretation I Myself have given. Say: every latter thing returns to Me, while whatever is beneath that returns to the Letters of Negation. This is the knowledge of the Bayān, if you understand. Then goodness is remembered unto the furthest limit of God in the knowledge of the reverent. Beneath goodness is the limit of God according to what you testify regarding those below, for the sincere ones. Let them recite the first verse if you are able. All of that is like this, if you understand. All of it is the Most Holy Name in the final returnings. You witness that as “He Whom God Shall Manifest,” if God wills, you shall come to certainty.

Then in the fourth: there is nothing in the harmonies of the Book unless you believe in Him Whom God Shall Manifest.

Then in the fifth: there is not a single letter revealed in the Bayān except that it possesses a spirit. Through the knowledge of distance you grieve, and through the knowledge of nearness you rejoice.

If you recite the negation, you annihilate them. This is what bears fruit with God, if you comprehend. And if you recite the affirmation in order to establish it firmly, this is what bears fruit with God, if you are capable. The first principle alone is that through the permission of God you draw near. All letters return to these two, if you perceive. Do not merely say, “There is no god but God,” while failing to unveil the throne of the light of affirmation.

