God has accepted from you, and this is the good-pleasure of God for those drawn near unto Him.

Then in the sixth: We have not revealed any remembrance of goodness in the Bayān except for Him Whom We shall manifest on the Day of Resurrection through My verses, so that you may behold Him. Nor is there any mention apart from goodness except concerning one who does not prostrate before Him, that you might make him among those who bow down. The Qurʾān was likewise revealed before this, yet you remained veiled from My intention. This is that around which night and day have circled through eight unities, while through it you unite in worship. Yet after its decree had been fulfilled, you remained veiled from its mystery. This is the balance of guidance within the Bayān. You believe in it until the time when the Sun of the Most High rises—that is, He Whom God Shall Manifest. If you truly know, then you will believe in Him, and you shall abide eternally in paradise. Otherwise, you are among those who perish.

Then in the seventh: the Day of Resurrection, according to what you understand, extends from the moment the Sun of Bahāʾ rises until it sets. This is better in the Book of God than the entirety of the night, if you comprehend. God has not created anything except for that Day, for on that Day all shall come to know the meeting with God and then His good-pleasure. On the Day of Resurrection this outward reality becomes understood. Will they not then look? Truly, We have been waiting. But God knows your condition. The decline has drawn near, yet on that Day you will not recognize it. Whoever’s meeting is the very essence of My meeting—do not be pleased for him with merely what one soul is pleased with for another soul. Rather, remember the final letter, and then you shall know your own limit.

