Then in the eighth: I have ordained death upon all things at the time of My manifestation for whatever lies outside My love. Whatever I initiate from My Cause—that alone benefits you and leads you from fire into light. That is the highest horizon, if you comprehend. That is death within life, and it is the truth without doubt. The death of the body is likewise similar to that death, if you perceive both of them within the reality of life.

Then in the ninth: concerning the Letter Sīn—everyone commanded by it on the Day of Resurrection shall be raised up. Say: this is indeed the truth, without doubt. Through the utterance of the Point they are raised. Such is the decree of the All-Encompassing, the Self-Subsisting.

Then in the tenth: what the servant is questioned about becomes manifest—just as he is questioned within the two graves, if you answer truthfully. This is the speech of the angel from God, if you possess certainty in the verses of God. These are the verses of Him Whom God Shall Manifest. Then through the shadow of the ninth, like the shadow of the tenth, you derive understanding.

Then the one after the ten: resurrection is true, like the grave. God raises up whomsoever He wills from among the living souls of His creation according to the judgment of the Manifestation of His own Self. Thus on the Day of Resurrection you too are raised by whatever He Whom God Shall Manifest speaks.

Then the second after the ten: the remembrance of the true path, and through it you shall pass. This is the command of Him Whom God Shall Manifest, if on the Day of Manifestation you act according to it. Say: all who came before awaited My Day. Then when I appeared, it was through Me that their religion was confirmed.

