What is there at the Path? All stand there waiting. That is their silence before the Truth, if you comprehend.

Then the third after the ten: the remembrance of the Balance. That is the very Self of Him Whom God Shall Manifest. Truth turns with Him just as a shadow turns with the sun. Then after the setting, you are left with the Bayān and the witnesses.

Then the fourth after the ten: the remembrance of the Reckoning. Like the Balance, it is truth. Everything revealed in the Bayān is that through which God brings humanity and all things to account. O My servants, be mindful.

Then the fifth after the ten: the Book is truth. That is the utterance of God from My tongue. Through the truth you shall attain certainty.

Then the sixth after the twenty: paradise is the love of God and then His good-pleasure. That is truly the truth, beyond all comparison. Truly, We abide therein eternally. Whatever is attributed to Me in paradise is attributed to Him Whom God Shall Manifest. Will you not then enter? As for the fire before it is transformed into light—that is the fire of God. It is Him Whom God Shall Manifest before He makes His own self known to you. You enter into the fire of love, and this is truly real, not merely metaphorical speech. If you enter, then you shall perceive every good thing.

Then the seventh after the ten: the remembrance of the fire. I do not love the mention of one who has not believed in Him Whom God Shall Manifest. Such a one—before belief is attributed to him—is attributed to the fire. O My servants, beware.

Then the eighth after the ten: the Hour. Through what God has explained in the Word, if God wills, you shall come to certainty.

