Do not invent things from yourselves and then make matters easier upon yourselves through artificiality.

Then the first after the ten: do not transgress the limits of the Bayān lest you suffer loss. Do not bring sorrow upon any soul, for this is among the greatest boundaries, so that you may not grieve Him Whom We shall manifest. Whoever transgresses shall not be judged as guided, for none brings true guidance except Him Whom We shall manifest through guidance itself. Say: O people of guidance, through My guidance be rightly guided.

Then the second after the ten: O My servants, descend throughout the regions of the earth, then direct whatever is therein according to the First Unity.

Then the third after the ten: O My servants, raise up the seats of the Unity according to whatever capacity you possess.

Then the fourth after the ten: O My servants, if you seek refuge in those lands, you shall find safety among the people, and they shall not gain power over you. Thus shall you seek refuge on the Day of Resurrection in the one raised from his resting place—not as on that Day when you seek refuge through others. Upon you rests the duty to act in such a way that the heavens and the earth and all that lies between them would almost break apart when they hear it. What is wrong with you? How is it that you do not understand?

Then the fifth after the ten: do not prevent anyone who seeks refuge in God and then in the Letters of the Living at the time of the latter manifestation; and before that, judge according to the former manifestation. Likewise, if someone seeks refuge with even a single person under protection, then for him to be killed in that person’s path is better before God than for you to reject him. O My servants, grant protection and refuge.

