Indeed, I am God. There is no god except Me, the Most Ancient, the Most Ancient. I revealed in the first gate of the fifth unity that you should raise up the sanctuary at the place where I was born, according to the extent of your ability.

Then the second: by My permission you shall raise up the sanctuaries of the Living, and place within them as many lamps as you desire.

Then the third: We have made the year nineteen months, so that perhaps you may walk within the Unity.

Then the fourth: you shall be named by My names, and We have called you “My Splendor (Bahāʾī).” Say: O My creation, direct yourselves toward Me. Name yourselves with the names Muḥammad, ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, then Ḥusayn, then Mahdī and Hādī. We have assigned a name to every letter of your name.

Say: all belong to Me, and I belong to God, My Lord. There is no god except God.

That is the Sovereign of the worlds.\
That is the Beloved of the worlds.\
That is the Pivot of the worlds.\
That is the Goal of the worlds.\
That is the One worshipped by the worlds.\
That is the One sought by the worlds.

That is your God and your King, then your Lord and your Possessor, then your Sovereign and your Owner, then the One described by all worlds.

Then the fifth: take from those who have not entered into the Bayān whatever pertains to them. Then if they believe, restore it to them, except in lands over which you have no authority.

Then the sixth: if a land is opened in the Bayān, then from it there shall be taken what has no equivalent, according to what has been commanded, and it shall be preserved.

