Then the ninth after the ten: the measure you value is nineteen portions of gold and silver. The Sovereign shall establish the first level of *Bahāʾ* at ten thousand dīnārs and the second at one thousand dīnārs. If each category becomes smaller, it shall not depart from its established limit. Below that, you shall not dispose of your possessions, and nothing is due from one whose holdings fall beneath it. Likewise, nothing is due from one whose possessions have not reached the amount of five hundred and forty mithqāls and upon which a full year has not passed. This is a bounty from Us so that you may give thanks. After that, if you find wealth that does not exceed the limits of the Bayān, then you shall bring from every mithqāl of gold five hundred dīnārs, and from every mithqāl of silver five dīnārs.

