Contemporary English:

When mutual contentment is found between them, then guard yourselves from separation, and through elevation you shall rise. Each one shall say:

“We are all content with God.”

God has made all the jewels of the earth the marriage-gift for the one I created for Him Whom We shall manifest. This is a grace from God upon him so that he may be among the thankful.

Then the eighth: do not seek proof except through the verses. Whoever does not seek proof through them possesses no knowledge. Do not mention miracles apart from them, so that perhaps on the Day of My manifestation you may immediately believe. Recite this continually and place it before your eyes so that on the Day of My manifestation you may not remain veiled.

Then the ninth: wear garments of silk on occasions of joy and prosperity. If you have the means for it, do not wear anything beneath its standard. The things by which you live privately for your comfort you may fashion from gold and silver. If you do not find the means for that, do not grieve, for truly I am your Lord. I shall come to you in your latter days if you believe in My verses.

Then the tenth: place red agate upon your hands and engrave upon it:

“Indeed, Him Whom God shall manifest is Truth, without doubt, and through Him all things are created and unto Him all things belong.”

Say:

“God is Truth, and whatever is besides God is creation, and all worship Him.”

Then the first after the ten:

“O Muḥammad, my teacher, do not cause me harm before five years have been completed.”

