Contemporary English:

...and not even in the blink of an eye should my heart be distressed thereafter. Do not bring me outside the bounds of dignity. If you intend punishment, do not exceed five strikes, and do not strike upon the flesh except with some barrier between them. If suffering results, your spouse becomes forbidden to you for nineteen days if you have forgotten. If you have no companion, then spend nineteen mithqāls of gold corresponding to what you inflicted, if you desire to be among the believers. Do not strike except lightly, very lightly. Seat children upon a bed, throne, or chair, for this is not considered among excesses toward them. Permit them what brings them joy.

Learn the *Shikastah* script, for God has made it a gate of His own self among forms of writing, so that perhaps you may write in such a way that your hearts are moved from stillness and you may become like flowing water for Him Whom We shall manifest. When your eyes behold Him, He will draw you as We have written. I have joined you with one who inherits, so that the throne of your Lord may not grieve in the dust of smallness, and all through Him shall not grieve. Say: if you had witnessed, I would have cut off from you what I had granted you from My dominion. O My servants, be mindful.

Then the second after the ten:

Do not approach the Ṭāʾ and the Qāf, and if necessity compels you, then endure for a full year.
